-- title:
--   Layered rational node rings with crossing presentations
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $5 \le q$, $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $F$ denotes the field `fieldBar q M'`, the intermediate field `xHFunctionFieldBar (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` of $\overline{\mathbb Q} \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$.
--
--   *Constants.* $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in `A.nonunits`; $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ has image in $A$. Write $A_0 :=$ `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))` for the induced valuation subring of $k_0$. The hypotheses `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres` require that $A_0$ be a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$, that $A_0$ be a Henselian local ring, and that its residue field be algebraically closed; `hκ` requires that every element of $A$ be congruent, modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   *Layers.* $\iota$ is an index type, $K : \iota \to$ intermediate fields of $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with each $K_n$ finite over $k_0$ (`hKfin`), $A_n$ is a valuation subring of $K_n$ with $x \in A_n$ iff $x \in A$ (`hAn`), and $n_0$ is an index with $K_{n_0} \le K_n$ for all $n$ (`hn₀`).
--
--   *Level field.* $F$ is made a $k_0$-algebra through $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q} \subseteq F$, and $F_0$ is an intermediate field of $k_0 \subseteq F$ subject to two hypotheses: the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is all of $F$; and a linear-disjointness clause, namely for every intermediate field $K'$ of $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ finite over $k_0$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and every $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to F$ whose values lie in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, if $c$ is $K'$-linearly independent and $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ in $F$, then all $a_i = 0$.
--
--   *Valuation subring and node ring at the base.* $W_0$ is a valuation subring of $F_0$ such that an element of $k_0$ lies in $A$ exactly when its image lies in $W_0$, $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring, and its maximal ideal is generated by the image of $\pi_0$. $O$ is a subring of $F_0$, local and noetherian, with: $O \subseteq W_0$; an element of $k_0$ lies in $A$ exactly when its image lies in $O$; for every $f \in O$ there is $x \in k_0$ with $x \in A$, image in $O$, such that $f - x$ is not a unit of $O$ (rationality of the residue field of $O$); and every element of $F_0$ is of the form $g/h$ with $g, h \in O$, $h \ne 0$.
--
--   *Crossing presentation at the base.* $E_0 \ge 1$ is a natural number, the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $O$ (`hπO`), $c_x, c_y \in O$, $u \in O^\times$, and $\iota_O$ is a ring isomorphism from the adic completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal onto the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` of the adic completion $\widehat{A_0}$ at the element $\pi_0^{E_0}$, that is, the quotient of the two-variable power series ring over $\widehat{A_0}$ by the ideal `uvCrossingIdeal`, with its distinguished elements `U`, `V` and its constants `const`; $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ are units of this model. The clauses are: $c_x c_y = \pi_0^{E_0} u$ in $O$; $\iota_O$ carries the image of each $x \in k_0 \cap A$ to `const` of the corresponding element of $\widehat{A_0}$; $\iota_O(c_x) = \gamma_U \cdot U$ and $\iota_O(c_y) = \gamma_V \cdot V$; $c_y$ lies in $W_0$ and indeed in the maximal ideal of $W_0$, while $c_x$, whenever it lies in $W_0$, lies outside the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   *Hasse germ.* The Laurent series [`ModularCurve.jqNModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18), obtained from `jqModC` by the substitution `qExpand … q`, lies in $F$ (`hJK`); $a_0 \in k_0$; the difference $j - a_0$ lies in $F_0$ (`hjF`) and in $O$ (`hjO`); and there are $e_J \ge 1$ and a unit $w_V$ of the base crossing model with $\iota_O(j - a_0) = w_V \cdot V^{e_J}$.
--
--   *Node-adapted chart at the base.* $B_x$ is a subring of $F_0$ with $B_x \subseteq O$, such that $f \in O$ iff $f = g/h$ for some $g, h \in B_x$ with $h$ a unit of $O$ whenever it lies in $O$, and such that for some finite set $T \subseteq F_0$, $B_x$ is the subring generated by $T$ together with the images of the elements of $k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   *The two ends.* First, a field $FI$ with an algebra structure over the residue field of $A$, a `RegularProlongation A ↥(fieldBar q M') FI` $R_x$ — that is, a valuation subring `Rx.integers` of $F$ together with a surjective ring map `Rx.residue` onto $FI$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, inducing $A$ on $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, compatible with the residue map of $A$, and such that every nonzero $f \in F$ has a scalar multiple in `Rx.integers` with nonzero residue — and a place $b_x$ of $FI$ over the residue field of $A$, i.e. a proper valuation subring containing the image of that residue field and which is a principal ideal ring. It is assumed that $b_x$ is rational (the residue field of $A$ surjects onto the residue field of $b_x$), that $O$ maps into `Rx.integers`, that residues of elements of $O$ lie in $b_x$, that non-units of $O$ have residue in the maximal ideal of $b_x$, that the residue of $c_x$ is $0$, and that the $b_x$-order (`Place.ord`) of the residue of $c_y$ equals $1$. Secondly, the same data $FSS$, $R$, $nd$ with: an element of $F_0$ lies in `R.integers` exactly when it lies in $W_0$; $nd$ rational; residues of elements of $O$ lie in $nd$; non-units of $O$ have residue in the maximal ideal of $nd$; the residue of $c_y$ is $0$; and the $nd$-order of the residue of $c_x$ equals $1$.
--
--   *Places and the ambient node ring.* $S$ is a set of places of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ characterised as the places dominating $O$: $P \in S$ iff $O$ maps into the valuation subring of $P$ and for every non-unit $f$ of $O$ the value `P.evalAt f` lies in $A$ and in the maximal ideal of $A$; moreover every $P \in S$ is rational. $\mathcal N$ is a subring of $F$ consisting exactly of the elements lying in `Rx.integers`, in `R.integers` and in the valuation subring of every $P \in S$; and `P.evalAt f` lies in $A$ for every $f \in \mathcal N$ and $P \in S$.
--
--   *Layer constants and their completions.* $C' : \iota \to$ subrings of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, contained in $A$, each a domain and a discrete valuation ring, with elements $\varpi'_l \in C'_l$; $W_c : \iota \to$ types, each a commutative domain, a discrete valuation ring, and adically complete for its maximal ideal, with elements $\pi_l$, natural numbers $e_L(l)$, and ring maps $j_l : C'_l \to W_c\,l$. The clauses are: $c \in C'_l$ iff $c \in A$ and $c$ lies in the image of $K_l$; for $d \in C'_l$, the residue of $d$ in $A$ vanishes iff $d \in \varpi'_l C'_l$; $C'_{n_0} \le C'_l$; $\pi_l$ is irreducible; there is $v$ with $v, v^{-1} \in C'_l$ and $\pi_0 = v \cdot \varpi_l'^{\,e_L(l)}$; $j_l(\varpi'_l) = \pi_l$; $j_l(c) \in (\pi_l^n)$ implies $c \in (\varpi_l'^{\,n})$; and every $w \in W_c\,l$ is congruent to some $j_l(c)$ modulo $\pi_l^n$.
--
--   *Conclusion.* There exists a family $\mathcal N_0 : \iota \to$ subrings of $F$, together with witnesses that each $\mathcal N_0(l)$ is a local ring and a noetherian ring, such that:
--
--   (1) every element of $O$ has image in $\mathcal N_0(n_0)$;
--
--   (2) an element of $O$ which is not a unit of $O$ has image which is not a unit of $\mathcal N_0(n_0)$;
--
--   (3) for every $f \in F$ there are $n$, $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$, $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to \mathcal N_0(n_0)$ and $b \in \mathcal N_0(n_0)$ with $b \ne 0$ in $F$ and $f \cdot b = \sum_i c_i \cdot a_i$;
--
--   (4) for every layer $l$, all of the following hold:
--    (a) $\mathcal N_0(n_0) \le \mathcal N_0(l) \le \mathcal N$;
--    (b) $S$ is exactly the set of places dominating $\mathcal N_0(l)$: $P \in S$ iff $\mathcal N_0(l)$ is contained in the valuation subring of $P$ and for every non-unit $f$ of $\mathcal N_0(l)$ the value `P.evalAt f` lies in $A$ and in the maximal ideal of $A$;
--    (c) the image of $C'_l$ in $F$ lies in $\mathcal N_0(l)$;
--    (d) for every $g \in \mathcal N_0(l)$ there is $o \in C'_l$ whose image lies in $\mathcal N_0(l)$ with $g - o$ not a unit of $\mathcal N_0(l)$;
--    (e) for all $n$, every $C'_l$-linearly independent $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and every $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to \mathcal N_0(l)$ with $\sum_i c_i \cdot a_i = 0$ in $F$ has all $a_i = 0$;
--    (f) there is a subring $B_x$ of $F$ contained in $\mathcal N_0(l)$, containing the images of $c_x$, $c_y$ and $u$, such that $f \in \mathcal N_0(l)$ iff $f = g/h$ with $g, h \in B_x$ and $h$ a unit of $\mathcal N_0(l)$ whenever it lies there, and such that for some finite set $T \subseteq F$, $B_x$ is the subring generated by $T$ together with the image of $C'_l$;
--    (g) the images of $c_x$ and $c_y$ lie in $\mathcal N_0(l)$, and the image of $u$ lies in $\mathcal N_0(l)$ and is a unit there;
--    (h) there exist a ring map $\sigma : W_c\,l \to \widehat{\mathcal N_0(l)}$ into the adic completion of $\mathcal N_0(l)$ at its maximal ideal and a ring isomorphism $\iota_c$ from $\widehat{\mathcal N_0(l)}$ onto the crossing model `UVCrossingModel (Wc l) (π l ^ (eL l * E₀))` such that: $\sigma(\pi_l)$ is the image of $\varpi'_l$ in $\widehat{\mathcal N_0(l)}$ (whenever that image lies in $\mathcal N_0(l)$); $\iota_c(\sigma(o)) =$ `const` $o$ for all $o \in W_c\,l$; the Hasse germ clause holds, namely $j - a_0$ lies in $\mathcal N_0(l)$ and there are $e \ge 1$ and a unit $w$ of the model with $\iota_c(j - a_0) = w \cdot V^{e}$; every element of $C'_l$, viewed in $\mathcal N_0(l)$, is of the form $\sigma(o)$ for some $o \in W_c\,l$; and the two residue laws hold, i.e. for $f \in \mathcal N_0(l)$ and $n \in \mathbb N$, if $f \in$ `Rx.integers` with nonzero `Rx.residue` of $b_x$-order $n$, then there is a unit $\gamma$ of the model with $\iota_c(f) - \gamma \cdot V^{n}$ in the ideal generated by `const` $\pi_l$ and `U`, and symmetrically, if $f \in$ `R.integers` with nonzero `R.residue` of $nd$-order $n$, then there is a unit $\gamma$ of the model with $\iota_c(f) - \gamma \cdot U^{n}$ in the ideal generated by `const` $\pi_l$ and `V`.
--
--   This is the layered form of the construction of a rational local node ring inside the function field of the full-level modular curve at a prime $q \ge 5$: from one node together with data for its two ends it produces, over every finite layer $K_l$ of constants, a local noetherian subring whose completion carries a $UV$-crossing presentation with exponent multiplied by the ramification index $e_L(l)$, together with the germ of $j - a_0$ and the order-matching residue laws at the two ends. It is used by the assembly of node centres and node charts for the semistable model, in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_nodeCentre_igusaEnd_layeredNodeRings_of_mem_nodes_igusaSep_layerExponent`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_nodeCentre_igusaEnd_layeredNodeRings_of_mem_nodes_igusaSep_layerExponent) and [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.klevel_nodeCore_nodeCharts_hasseGerm_nodeCentre_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.klevel_nodeCore_nodeCharts_hasseGerm_nodeCentre_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep).
